    "limits": "Requires browser WebCodecs and OPFS in a secure context. Encoding waits for every frame and verifies packet/sample counts. Browser termination, memory exhaustion or codec failure aborts export; no promise of binary identity to a lossy screen recording.",
    "safariCompatibility": "Each export document loads independent CSS FontFaces from identical embedded font bytes; no cross-document FontFaceSet.add. Frame indices and intended timestamps are verified separately, with a 2-microsecond tolerance for WebKit Canvas VideoFrame timestamp conversion, and explicit sample timing for the muxer.",
    "savedVideos": "Native OPFS File downloads without whole-file JS copies; completed MP4s and per-file metadata survive reloads. Finalized legacy/orphan files are recovered from bounded header/footer reads. No automatic deletion of successful exports. Large and 2160P/120 exports bypass platform file sharing. Actions unlock only after GPU, encoder and audio cleanup.",
    "speed": "Benchmark native AVC/HEVC hardware candidates and both encoder latency modes at the selected resolution; retain only candidates emitting every test frame, cache the fastest for this browser/preset. Bounded two-frame render/encode pipeline; combine audio/video RPC with contiguous ~100 ms PCM batches. Preserve original output compositing and bitrate. No resolution, shader, frame or glyph reduction. Bundled AAC encoder preserves codec priming PTS for consistent gapless, synchronized output across Safari devices."
